{:tier :glm-5.2, :verse 22, :comments ["<b>If you afflict him.</b> Rashi's comment: he pronounced a decree but did not mention its punishment if the afflicted one remains silent — but 'and it shall be, if he cries out to Me, I will hear, for I am gracious' etc. <b>For if he cries out.</b> Perhaps he is deserving, and he will cry out to Me — I will hear." "<b>Cry out, he will cry out.</b> It speaks of the orphan, whose way is to be young and not of understanding age to make his humiliation known like the widow, but the law of the widow is the same." "<b>I will hear his cry.</b> For by law, the one who afflicts receives lashes."], :book :exodus, :voice :chizkuni, :lang :en, :chapter 22, :notes {0 "The comment 'גזם ולא הזכיר ענשו כשישתוק העני' paraphrases Rashi on this verse; 'והיה אם יצעק' is the compiler's own transition to the next phrase of the verse. The clause 'דילמא שמא הוא ראוי' appears to be the compiler's own reasoning."}, :source-witnesses [{"versionTitle" "Sefaria community Hebrew (PD)", "language" "he"}], :timestamp "2026-07-30T14:59:52.156025336Z", :translated-from :he, :model "glm-5.2"}